.\" Title: vrc-list
.\" Author: vrc contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\"
.TH VRL\-LIST 1 "2025" "vrc" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrc list \- list running vrc instances and their commands

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrc
\fBlist\fR [\fB\-\-target\fR \fIPID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists all running vrc instances. For each instance, connects to its UDS control socket to retrieve the live command list from memory, including commands added dynamically via \fBvrc spawn\-in\fR.

The output shows each instance with its PID, daemon/display status, and uptime, followed by a list of commands with their PIDs, names, and running status.

When \fB\-\-target\fR is specified, only the specified instance is shown.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-\-target " " \fIPID\fR
Only show the instance with the given PID.

.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Present a numbered list of running instances and let the user select
which ones to show by typing space-separated numbers (e.g. "1 3 5").
Requires a terminal (stdin must be a TTY).

.SH OUTPUT

Instance header line: INSTANCE PID: N DAEMON: yes/no DISPLAY: yes/no UP: duration

Per command: PID (indented) command_name STATUS: running|frozen|exited duration

.SH EXAMPLES

List all instances:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc list\fR
INSTANCE  PID: 12345  DAEMON: no  DISPLAY: yes  UP: 3m 15s
  5678     htop                          STATUS: running  3m 15s
.fi
.RE

List a specific instance:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc list \-\-target 12345\fR
.fi
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vrc (1),
.BR vrc\-stop (1),
.BR vrc\-spawn\-in (1),
.BR vrc\-keys (1)
